# Allen Relation: MEETS / MET-BY
#
# MEETS: interval A ends at the exact moment interval B begins.
#   A meets B  iff  A.end = B.start
#
# MET-BY: the symmetric inverse — B is met-by A.
#   B met-by A  iff  B.start = A.end
#
# Legal patterns that trigger MEETS:
#   "whilst awaiting [...] coming into force of the amended Agreement"
#   "provisionally applied until [...] enters into force"
#   "on the first day of the month following notification"
#   "the new agreement replaces the old agreement as of"
#   seamless succession of one legal regime by another
#
# Grounded example (en_contracts_seed1, Appendix VIII):
#   Provisional de facto application period [1.1.1995, entry_into_force)
#   MEETS formal agreement period [entry_into_force, expiry].
#   No gap and no overlap between the two validity periods.

```catala
declaration scope AllenMeets:
  input interval_a_start content date   # start of the first period
  input interval_a_end content date     # end of the first period
  input interval_b_start content date   # start of the succeeding period
  input interval_b_end content date     # end of the succeeding period
  output is_meets content boolean       # A ends exactly when B starts
  output is_met_by content boolean      # B starts exactly when A ends (symmetric)
```

## MEETS

Interval A ends at the exact moment interval B begins.

```catala
scope AllenMeets:
  date round down
  definition is_meets equals
    interval_a_end = interval_b_start
```

## MET-BY

The symmetric statement from B's perspective.

```catala
scope AllenMeets:
  definition is_met_by equals
    interval_b_start = interval_a_end
```
